= Opening of the Constituyent Cortes

Following the Constituyent Elections of June 28, the elected deputies 
meet in the Cortes to prepare and discuss a Constitution that governs the republican regime. The Republican-Socialist Conjunction has a very large majority thanks to the disorganization of the monarchical forces.

The jurist Adolfo Posada has delivered a first draft based on the Spanish 1812, 1837 and 1869 liberal constitutions and in the german 1919's Constitution. The highlights are the concept of autonomies as a middle point between a unitary and a fededral State, a secularism that recognizes a preferential place of the Catholic Church and bicameral Cortes. Both the Catholic Church and most of the republican and socialist parties opposed this draft, beings the only exception the DLR.

After this backlash, a new Constitutional Comission lead by the socialist jurist Jiménez de Asúa was created. The new draft created a socially progressive Constitution that maintained the autonomies but implemented a much more radical secularism with the suppression of religious orders and the nationalization of their assets, and unciameral Cortes.


- @hope: Let's hope the Conjunction stands together until the Constitution is drafted.

